e UI more discoverable (especially on desktop; on tablet, along-press could trigger the same via the touch handlers as hinted in the mobile guide).Visual Cues: Enhance node and connection visuals for clarity. For example, currently all nodes havethe same style (gray box). We propose coloring nodes by category or status: e.g., audio objects haveone color, MIDI objects another, Live API/UI objects another (the technical spec gives examples: osc~ generator = wheat color, filter~ = sky blue, etc.). We can define a color palette fornode types (maybe aligning with the electric teal or orange for certain categories). Also, when anobject is active or producing sound, its outline or background might glow subtly (or an LEDindicator on the node) – giving real-time feedback in the patch. Connections (wires) can also reflectstatus: perhaps animate or glow for active signals (for MIDI, maybe a small moving dot; for audio,maybe a faint pulse).Max-like Appearance: To feel familiar to Max users, nodes should display more than just a labelwhen possible. E.g., if a node represents a UI element like live.dial, showing an actual knobicon or graphical representation on the node would be ideal. At minimum, including the object’sarguments/parameters in the label (already done, e.g., “metro 500” label includes the 500 argument) and eventually sliders or dials for those with UI (perhaps in the Inspector panel or inline onnode). Each node could also show small inlet/outlet ports (currently just the single top/bottom).The Enhanced node architecture will support multiple inlets/outlets with handles spaced out,which we will implement so objects like dac~ with 2 inlets, 2 outlets render properly. This requires• • • 48• • • 6364• 6566• 6768697
